What I Learned

Through this project, I learned how VPC CIDRs, subnet associations, route tables, VPC Peering, 
and security groups work together to enable private communication between AWS networks. 
I gained practical experience accessing private EC2 instances through a bastion host, configuring SSH ProxyJump,
and validating connectivity with forward and reverse ping tests. The controlled ICMP failure also taught me
to troubleshoot systematically instead of assuming that an active peering connection guarantees reachability.
Finally, I learned the importance of cleaning up cloud resources after a lab to avoid unnecessary costs.

